  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unsettled weather will persist throughout this week with \ndaily chances of showers and thunderstorms. Some storms may be\nstrong to severe, and multiple rounds of thunderstorms may\nincrease the flash flood threat throughout the week. \n\nAn upper level ridge currently remaining quasi-stationary across\nthe western Conus will lead to subtle troughing across the\nNortheast and Mid-Atlantic states through much of this week.\nThis northwest flow pattern combined with a 50-80 knot jet\nstreak remaining in place across Pennsylvania and states north \nwill aid in deep layer shear present across the region. This \nshear coupled with mid level disturbances traveling in the mean \nnorthwest flow around the western Conus ridge east through the \nOhio valley will lead to possible repeated rounds of Mesoscale \nConvective Systems (MCS) moving into the region throughout the \nweek. Some of these MCS may produce strong to severe wind gusts \nthat have already been seen across the area on Monday with one \nof these MCS. Overall, there is much uncertainty with the timing\nof these thunderstorm complexes, as some may enter the region \nthrough the overnight or early morning hours; however, the \ntiming of when they come through the region will greatly \ndetermine how strong the winds will be as they move into the \nregion. \n\nAlong with the severe thunderstorm potential, there will also be\na flash flood threat across the region. With multiple rounds of\nstorms possible, some areas could receive several inches of\nrainfall by the end of the week, which may lead to swelling of\nstreams and creeks across the region. Urban flooding also can't\nbe ruled out, especially with any storms that track over\nrepeated locations. A large concern is that these aforementioned\nsystems leave trailing outflow boundaries draped across the\narea in the morning, which may then trigger afternoon showers\nand thunderstorms during the afternoon and evening hours. Given\nthis flash flood threat, a Flood Watch has been issued across\nareas along and west of the Blue Ridge through Thursday morning,\nwith extensions in time possibly needed depending on future\nforecasts.",
